# File: scripts/__tests__/sdlc-execute.test.mjs
#
# Generated from: specs/216-honor-passed-worker-handoff-after-prompt-wait-failure/requirements.md
Feature: Honor passed worker handoff after prompt wait failure
  The execute controller previously treated a non-success
  herdr agent prompt --wait as worker_failed before reading
  a matching passed idle/done handoff. This was fixed by
  making the on-disk handoff plus idle/done state authoritative.

  # --- Bug Is Fixed ---

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: Prompt wait failure does not override a passed idle start handoff
    Given a sibling start worker has written .omp/sdlc/handoffs/42-start.json as a valid passed non-intervention handoff
    And that worker is idle or done
    When herdr agent prompt s42-start ... --wait returns a non-success status
    Then execute does not persist failed.reasonCode worker_failed for start
    And it records start complete, closes the pane created for start, and continues to implement

  # --- Related Behavior Still Works ---

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: Missing invalid failed or busy start workers still fail closed
    Given a start worker whose handoff is missing, mismatched, invalid, failed, blocked, or intervention true, or whose agent state is not idle or done after the wait
    When execute evaluates that worker
    Then it stops non-zero, keeps that worker pane open, writes a failed run record
    And it notifies with Stopped on #42 start. Worker pane pane-1 agent s42-start left open.

  # --- Edge Case ---

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario: Re-running execute reuses the live passed start worker
    Given the same idle or done s42-start worker remains live with that passed non-intervention handoff
    When execute is invoked again for #42
    Then it advances past start and does not start a second start worker
